ral justice and accountability"}]}, {"id": "2ebdbc63-d5da-45af-bb2a-8bab6280ba8b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical uncertainty", "description": "Learners make defensible decisions even when evidence is incomplete.", "children": [{"id": "0ffb4ac7-5533-4eba-9f07-dd25085f6c52", "type": "concept", "title": "Precaution, uncertainty, contested values, and risk communication"}, {"id": "8072b669-0bf8-47b2-8250-cd655959f5fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Moral distress and disagreement"}, {"id": "f98ea5ec-730b-4d3f-976d-1f026b39677e", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation of rationale"}]}]}, {"id": "b124784d-f1e4-4a86-a3a2-a55d6a646dd8", "type": "topic", "title": "Individual Rights, Liberty, and the Public Good", "description": "Examine when public health may limit individual liberty and what safeguards make restrictions legitimate.", "children": [{"id": "c5612e94-f50a-47f4-9d3c-7b3275a57a56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rights in public health", "description": "Students examine how liberty, privacy, bodily integrity, speech, religion, and equality arise in public health policy.", "children": [{"id": "be6d3caa-2a18-4cb8-8ff9-f0134e451806", "type": "concept", "title": "Constitutional rights and statutory protections"}, {"id": "797e906f-000e-4567-8a8b-506bf2ec8203", "type": "concept", "title": "Due process and equal protection concepts"}, {"id": "f84b2ed1-5baa-4d7d-b8dc-98382283b3d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Reasonable limits and public justification"}]}, {"id": "956f9838-f754-41d6-a8fa-1311d316d682", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public good and collective risk", "description": "The gist is to understand why individual choices can create population-level consequences.", "children": [{"id": "cd64109a-957a-42ba-9ede-db7b6ea8ddcc", "type": "concept", "title": "Externalities, herd protection, environmental exposure, and communicable disease"}, {"id": "e8563912-9dcd-4c17-b2fb-63f73f2fe7b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Free rider problems"}, {"id": "11568007-b28c