ance, and outcomes"}, {"id": "bc84bb71-9a1b-41bf-b8b5-78f243e6672d", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity effects and unintended consequences"}, {"id": "c2215433-3739-46bb-9abd-e01d9b09b860", "type": "concept", "title": "Data sources and measurement limits"}]}, {"id": "2924a799-f257-4609-a749-bf626231423d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Law as intervention", "description": "Learners see law as a public health tool that must be designed and evaluated.", "children": [{"id": "80d336b2-0899-4d11-899b-9434133b4200", "type": "concept", "title": "Taxes, bans, mandates, licensing, zoning, labeling, and standards"}, {"id": "0bbe4406-e37f-4210-a6e1-0f04970ed199", "type": "concept", "title": "Preemption and local innovation"}, {"id": "bd8cd24f-be81-4441-8f0e-f1711d2d7858", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence-informed policy design"}]}]}, {"id": "7aeb45c2-8986-4c35-bb62-e6740659d194", "type": "topic", "title": "Global Health Law, Human Rights, and International Governance", "description": "Connect domestic public health choices to global health law, human rights, and cross-border obligations.", "children": [{"id": "0fc0e917-de57-484a-9b24-ab33a290c769", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global health law foundations", "description": "Students connect domestic public health to international cooperation.", "children": [{"id": "4763025e-3776-44f9-995d-e5f2d0acd80b", "type": "concept", "title": "International Health Regulations, treaties, soft law, and global institutions"}, {"id": "733866c1-6f0d-4e13-8205-1d3bd54ee95d", "type": "concept", "title": "WHO, PAHO, WTO, and human rights bodies"}, {"id": "9b9d06a8-3bbc-4705-b021-356ee7eaefe8", "type": "concept", "title": "Sovereignty and cooperation"}]}, {"id": "d19b05c4-e086-49e8-9bf8-a794584651ee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Human rights and public health", "description": "This subtopic frames health as connected to dignity and legal obligations.", "children": [{"id": "d8594232-6f87-491f-9618-650f8d08e8e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Right to health, nondiscrimination, participation, accountability, and remedies"}, {"id": "656fca5b-a482-4c7e-9c9d-009e704d9591", "type": "concept", "title": "Restrictions on rights during emergencies"}, {"id": "0a44b5ce-228b-4b82-a815-b1a5c44b6a69", "type": "concept", "title": "Global equity and solidarity"}]}, {"id": "d597fab4-00f9-4f38-9208-9bab17a54094", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cross-border public health issues", "description": "Learners analyze problems no single jurisdiction can solve alone.", "children": [{"id": "f37a8b2c-9fe2-4084-a6d0-2a63c802e2c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Pandemics, migration, climate, tobacco, antimicrobial resistance, and access to medicines"}, {"id": "50156172-3f55-49db-9acc-92b39529237a", "type": "concept", "title": "Global surveillance and data sharing"}, {"id": "77d2cecd-dbea-4849-808e-ce74172bc8b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Colonialism, power, and equity"}]}]}, {"id": "5df61af8-9dca-49c1-ae93-5c1ed4083572", "type": "topic", "title": "Public Health Policy, Litigation, Advocacy, and Regulatory Strategy", "description": "Examine how statutes, regulations, litigation, and advocacy shape population health outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "711f21b9-e870-42c5-a6f7-7d82cd53f3a2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy tools", "description": "Students learn the legal levers available to public health practitioners.", "children": [{"id": "09f0149b-09b4-4c36-b4fa-1022d316b587", "type": "concept", "title": "Statutes, regulations, ordinances, guidance, funding conditions, enforcement, and litigation"}, {"id": "c8f35517-e496-4acd-8f29-665b9656f303", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative agencies and rulemaking"}, {"id": "eb941c24-6f40-49b1-a054-b51228ab7797", "type": "concept", "title": "Local, state, and federal strategy"}]}, {"id": "2a3ca5b8-8be3-4ec2-aca3-ab50d2de89a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Litigation and courts", "description": "The point is to understand how courts shape public health authority.", "children": [{"i